The same seed can play out very differently in Slay the Spire 2. That amazing seed you shared with a friend turns into a nightmare for them. A brutal seed ends your win streak, but feels easy when you replay it to see what went wrong...

This isn't just your imagination. The base game's code is so haphazard that any action can drastically change later results in seemingly unrelated areas. For example, an extra shuffle in one fight affects the next fight's opening hand, skipping a chest changes later card rewards, buying Royal Stamp first changes which cards War Paint upgrades, and fighting one more or one fewer battle completely changes every boss Rare-card reward.

Can this be fixed? Try Seedline.

With over 200 hours of design and refinement, Seedline rewrites all in-combat and out-of-combat random effects, eliminating all the sources of same-seed divergence described above.

This makes sharing great seeds more relatable, reviewing brutal seeds more useful, and same-seed competition fairer.

Just install it, then forget it's there. Compatible with commonly used mods and unnoticeable during play, it quietly protects your seed while you enjoy the game.

[b]Requirements[/b]

[list]
[*]Windows and StS2 v0.114.0 on public-beta.
[*]Standard and Dread single-player, custom modifiers: Flight, Murderous, Terminal, Night Terrors, Midas, Big Game Hunter, Character Cards, Hoarder and Draft.
[*]Seedline stays inactive in multiplayer, Blitz, Daily and runs with other modifiers.
[*]Supports modded characters, but is incompatible with Combat Solver.
[/list]

[b]Q&A[/b]

[b]Does this guarantee identical outcomes?[/b]
If all major decisions stay the same, yes! The catch is that Slay the Spire 2 has a lot of major decisions. So expect less divergence between same-seed runs, not a guarantee that they will never diverge.

[b]Does it change vanilla probabilities?[/b]
Yes. For example, we preserve vanilla Rare-card probabilities, but keeping card rewards consistent requires normal fights and elites to have the same Uncommon-card rates. This means elite rewards offer about 0.15 fewer Uncommon cards on average than in vanilla, while the overall Uncommon-card rate stays roughly the same. This is the mod's largest probability adjustment, but it is still small compared with the roughly 1.1 Uncommon cards you can expect to see in a single normal-fight reward.

[b]Doesn't Catfood already prevent same-seed divergence?[/b]
Catfood pioneered efforts to prevent same-seed divergence. Seedline offers broader coverage and focuses on preserving the vanilla experience, making it better suited to everyday and win-streak play.

[b]What's one difference between Seedline and Catfood?[/b]
Catfood separates card rewards by normal fights versus elites. Seedline separates them by whether the reward contains a Rare card.

[b]Can I use save/load to try different actions?[/b]
Yes, but save/load gives you far fewer ways to manipulate outcomes. This is a tradeoff for consistency: the actions that let you reroll results through save/load can also make same-seed runs diverge when you play without reloading. Better support for vanilla-style save/load play is planned.

[b]Do I need everything unlocked?[/b]
No. Seedline automatically uses fully unlocked content without changing your profile's unlock progress.

[b]Are other mods required?[/b]
No. Seedline runs independently. RitsuLib 0.6.15 fails to initialize on StS2 v0.114.0; this release is validated without it.

[b]Does it work with modded characters?[/b]
Most out-of-combat effects are supported, but most in-combat randomness, including shuffles, still follows the original rules.

[b]Can I enable or disable Seedline mid-run?[/b]
No. A Seedline run may load with Seedline disabled but show a black screen on Save and Quit.

[b]Where can I report a problem?[/b]
Leave a comment on this page or join QQ group 609823795. Include versions, enabled mods, and relevant logs or screenshots.

[b]Is this project open source?[/b]
Yes. The source code and detailed design are available on [url=https://github.com/asHOH/seedline]GitHub[/url]. Stars are welcome!

Design suggestions are welcome. I offer CNY 100 for each suggestion I adopt (excluding CARD_ORDER).

[b]Was this project written by AI?[/b]
For the design, 10% comes from mechanics already present in Catfood, 80% is my own, and only 10% comes from original AI ideas I adopted after discussing them with it. The code was entirely written by AI. However, designing this mod took more than ten times as long as writing the code. AI was frankly terrible at design, so I mainly used it to gather and organize information.

[b]What's planned next?[/b]
Support for vanilla-style save/load play, broader mod compatibility, designs for Blitz and multiplayer modes, and articles and videos explaining Seedline's design.
